    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="0794" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6200/17a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d875-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-03T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 4385, February 3, 2 p.m. Suspend all activities on behalf of Germany
                    until further instructions from Department or information is received from other
                    sources indicating which country will be entrusted with German interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d875-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d875-f1-content">
                <p>The same, with appropriate references, to the diplomatic representatives in
                    France, Greece, Japan, Portugal, Roumania, Morocco, Russia, and Egypt.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
